body: '## Session Overview\n\nContinuation of cross-study team verdict session. Previous session did research (4 external repos) and team analysis (Architect, Sage, Jinx, Sentinel shaped 6 features). This session implemented all 6.\n\n## Two Orchestrations\n\n### Orchestration 1: Security Prereqs + P1-P3 (v5.32.0)\n\nStage 0 (parallel):\n- [security] — 12 findings: 4 blocking (enforce allow-by-default, one-sided relay, missing prepareForPublish, raw sharedSecret), 4 high, 3 medium\n- [builder] — Implemented all features but missed 2 blocking security gaps\n\nOrchestrator intervention: Fixed enforce() handlers, outbox filtering, deny_content lists\n\nStage 1: [reviewer] — Confirmed spec compliance (gap narrations NOT in stop hook)\nStage 2: [documentor] — Registered #gap-narrator, #activity-metrics, #soft-provenance (1,240 symbols)\n\n### Orchestration 2: P4-P6 (v5.33.0)\n\nStage 0: [builder] — Implemented all 3 features, added aliases to 4 tools\nOrchestrator: Added aliases to 6 more tools (10 total)\nStage 1+2 (parallel): [reviewer] found getHealthDot rootDir bug, [documentor] registered 3 new components (1,243 symbols)\n\n## What Shipped\n\n### v5.32.0 — Security + P1-P3\n- 4 new ContentCategory values (gap_narrations, cost_data, health_status, execution_metrics)\n- RING1_CONTENT_CATEGORIES constant for project-locked enforcement\n- notebook-publish enforcement boundary (deny-by-default)\n- Bidirectional Symphony relay Ring 1 filtering (incoming + outbox)\n- shareability field on NotebookEntry + prepareForPublish()\n- Gap narrator: 13 templates, doctor --explain, postflight integration\n- Activity metrics: tool calls, payload size, duration per agent\n- Soft provenance: parentId + lineageType on NotebookEntry\n\n### v5.33.0 — P4-P6\n- Outcome reference tracking: notebook entry IDs per agent per orchestration\n- Compliance health: trend analysis + health dot in paradigm_status\n- Tool aliases: 10 tools aliased for LLM matching\n\n## Remaining\n- npm publish v5.31.0-5.33.0\n- No more cross-study features to implement — all 6 done'
